    <fr:title text="System L">System L</fr:title>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>
  The <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\lambda \bar {\lambda }\mu \tilde {\mu }]]></fr:tex> calculus has
  <html:ul><html:li>environments <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma ]]></fr:tex></html:li>
    <html:li>co-environments <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Delta ]]></fr:tex></html:li>
    <html:li>command judgements <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \vdash  \Delta ]]></fr:tex></html:li>
    <html:li>term judgements <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \vdash  A \mid  \Delta ]]></fr:tex></html:li>
    <html:li>context judgements <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \mid  A \vdash  \Delta ]]></fr:tex></html:li></html:ul></html:p>
    <html:p>
  The <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\lambda \bar {\lambda }\mu \tilde {\mu }]]></fr:tex> calculus is interpreted using the <fr:link href="/0003/" title="Continuation Monad" uri="https://forest.vikraman.org/0003/" display-uri="0003" type="local">continuation monad</fr:link> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[K = R^{R^{(\mathsf {-})}}]]></fr:tex>.
</html:p>
    <html:p>
  In call-by-value (CBV):
  <html:ul><html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma ]]></fr:tex> is interpreted as sums and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Delta ]]></fr:tex> as products of types.</html:li>
    <html:li>The function type is interpreted as <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A \to  R^{R^B}]]></fr:tex>, or <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R^{R^B \times  A}]]></fr:tex>, or <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R^B \to  R^A]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \vdash  \Delta ]]></fr:tex> is interpreted as <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \times  R^\Delta  \to  R]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \vdash  A \mid  \Delta ]]></fr:tex> is interpreted as <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \times  R^\Delta  \to  KA]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
    <html:ul><html:li>Values <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \vdash  A \mid  \Delta ]]></fr:tex> are interpreted as <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \times  R^\Delta  \to  A]]></fr:tex>.</html:li></html:ul>
    <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \mid  A \vdash  \Delta ]]></fr:tex> is interpreted as <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \times  R^\Delta  \to  R^A]]></fr:tex>.</html:li></html:ul></html:p>
    <html:p>
  In call-by-name (CBN):
  <html:ul><html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma ]]></fr:tex> is interpreted as products and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Delta ]]></fr:tex> as sums of types.</html:li>
    <html:li>The function type is interpreted as <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R^A \times  B]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \vdash  \Delta ]]></fr:tex> is interpreted as <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R^\Gamma  \times  \Delta  \to  R]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \vdash  A \mid  \Delta ]]></fr:tex> is interpreted as <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R^\Gamma  \times  \Delta  \to  R^A]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
    <html:li><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \mid  A \vdash  \Delta ]]></fr:tex> is interpreted as <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R^\Gamma  \times  \Delta  \to  KA]]></fr:tex>.</html:li>
    <html:ul><html:li>Covalues <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\Gamma  \mid  A \vdash  \Delta ]]></fr:tex> are interpreted as <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R^\Gamma  \times  \Delta  \to  A]]></fr:tex>.</html:li></html:ul></html:ul></html:p>
    <html:p>
  This induces an equational theory for fine-grained CBV <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\lambda \bar {\lambda }\mu \tilde {\mu }]]></fr:tex> and fine-grained CBN <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\lambda \bar {\lambda }\mu \tilde {\mu }]]></fr:tex>,
  that I have yet to define.
</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
